1
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,960
Don't hurt Rawee again.

2
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:43,000
Have you forgotten what they did to us?

3
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:44,720
But Rawee

4
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:46,880
is my own nephew, after all.

5
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:48,560
He's only nice to you

6
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:50,880
because he thinks you're Nada,

7
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:52,200
not Lada.

8
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:56,400
From the DNA test Ms. Pimpa
secretly had done on you and Aunt Da.

9
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:57,800
You know about that?

10
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:59,040
Yes.

11
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:02,000
And I've been waiting for you
to tell everyone.

12
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:05,880
How long will you keep posing
as Aunt Da's son?

13
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:10,240
Korn, hurry and pull me up!
I can't hold on much longer.

14
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:14,320
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Someone called about two guests</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">who came with you.</font></font></i>

15
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:16,960
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">One fell off a cliff,</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">and the other was shot.</font></font></i>

16
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:19,880
Uncle!

17
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:22,000
Uncle!

18
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:23,600
I couldn't save Wee in time.

19
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:26,360
Ms. Lada.

20
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:32,880
I've filed a police report.
They've ordered an immediate search.

21
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:36,520
The police are also on their way
to question Phakorn.

22
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:41,840
What's gotten into Thong?

23
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:44,080
I know, right?

24
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:47,360
I can understand why he'd be angry
with Jak for threatening me today.

25
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:48,640
But Rawee?

26
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:52,320
Thong knows Rawee is Nada's son.

27
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:57,680
I've even asked him not to hurt Rawee.

28
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:01,000
I don't think Thong would go so far
as to kill him.

29
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:06,680
Maybe it was an accident.

30
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:11,960
Or maybe Thong wasn't the one who did it.

31
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:17,480
That's impossible.

32
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:20,240
Those two brothers are very close.

33
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:24,400
Maybe Rawee's the only one who thinks so.

34
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:27,680
I think you've known for a long time

35
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:30,080
that I'm not your biological son.

36
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:33,560
But what's even stranger

37
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:36,840
is why the results show you and Wee

38
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:39,560
aren't mother and son.

39
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:42,120
Who are you really?

40
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:48,360
But you don't have to answer me.

41
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:50,760
What do you want?

42
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:54,760
Legally adopt me.

43
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:57,200
Then we won't need a DNA test
that could expose us.

44
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:01,440
I promise

45
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:03,760
this will stay between us

46
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:05,680
forever.

47
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:13,440
And one more thing. You should get it done
as soon as possible.

48
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:15,680
Because once Grandfather wakes up,

49
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:18,280
I'm not going down alone.

50
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:21,560
You're the one who did this

51
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:23,640
to my father, aren't you?

52
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:25,960
Are you sure he's your father?

53
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:31,480
Phakorn knows

54
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:35,520
they can use
the grandparents' DNA to prove it.

55
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:37,680
And if Rawee were out of the picture,

56
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:39,280
that would solve everything.

57
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:45,240
If what you suspect is true,

58
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:50,040
I'll never let that ungrateful brat
get away with it.

59
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:52,840
Thamrong.

60
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:57,160
Once the police have questioned Phakorn,
take him back to Bangkok right away.

61
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,280
Of course.

62
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:04,560
Please be okay, Rawee.

63
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:20,440
Thank you.

64
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:24,120
Have they found Wee yet?

65
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:27,760
I'm hurt too, you know.
Don't you even care?

66
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,320
What happened?

67
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:32,880
How did Wee fall off the cliff?

68
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:37,040
How did your brother fall off the cliff?

69
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,600
You were there, weren't you?

70
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:41,960
Wee went in to help Mr. Jak.
I barely made it out alive myself.

71
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:45,280
I don't know what got into that freak.

72
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:50,600
Ms. Alyssa, I'm planning
to take Phakorn back to Bangkok now.

73
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:51,960
You should come with us.

74
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:55,320
You go ahead, Uncle.

75
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:58,240
Why?

76
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:00,840
We still don't know
what he has against Uncle Jak.

77
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:04,520
You're his niece.
What if he comes back to hurt you?

78
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:08,240
I agree with Phakorn on this.

79
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:10,240
Better safe than sorry.

80
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:15,560
I want to stay
and wait for news about Wee.

81
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:21,320
You seem awfully worried about Wee.

82
00:08:22,400 --> 00:08:23,680
Aren't you worried about him?

83
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:28,400
Then I'll stay here instead.

84
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:31,200
You should go home
and wait for news, Ms. Alyssa.

85
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:32,880
If you don't go back,

86
00:08:33,559 --> 00:08:35,280
Mr. Nimit will be very upset with me.

87
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:36,880
I'll talk to Dad myself.

88
00:08:38,159 --> 00:08:40,799
Wee came here
because Dad and I wanted him to.

89
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:44,280
I can't leave until they find him.

90
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:48,720
Wee keeps getting hurt because of me.

91
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:52,880
If anything else happens to him,
I'll never forgive myself.

92
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:19,040
Wee!

93
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:26,160
Korn, hurry and pull me up.

94
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:40,800
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">We have to find a way to get you treated.</font></font></i>

95
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:43,920
This is the best solution.

96
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:49,440
You're her son. You could just ask her
to help me get treatment.

97
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:51,080
But if you're not her son,

98
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:54,000
she might not help us.

99
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:56,520
Once you're better,

100
00:10:57,680 --> 00:10:59,760
we can tell her the truth.

101
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:02,480
But if your surgery doesn't work,

102
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:06,480
she'll be able to take care of you
for the rest of your life.

103
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:12,600
I love you so much, Korn.

104
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:17,440
I'd do anything for my little brother.

105
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:22,960
We'll always take care of each other
until the day we die.

106
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:37,560
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I promise.</font></font></i>

107
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:42,680
I'll bring our family back
to the way it was when Dad was here.

108
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:51,120
I'll be here to see you succeed.

109
00:11:57,800 --> 00:12:00,400
Why do you make everything sound so easy?

110
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:02,520
Why make things harder than they are?

111
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:04,840
I won't let you struggle, Korn.

112
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:07,360
We're brothers, no matter what.

113
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:14,920
Hearing you say that
just makes me feel even guiltier.

114
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:18,320
I've treated you badly so many times.

115
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:20,800
You even punched me.

116
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:22,240
I was jealous.

117
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:24,720
I've told you a hundred times, Korn.

118
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:27,160
I don't have feelings for Ms. Alyssa.

119
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:33,600
But Alyssa might have feelings for you.

120
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:18,440
I've known you both since you were little.

121
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:21,040
I've loved you like my own family.

122
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:24,840
Today, I'll take your word for it.

123
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:29,320
But if I find out you're lying,

124
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:33,280
that you hurt Rawee for personal gain,

125
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:37,120
I won't let you get away with it.

126
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:42,280
I made you who you are today.

127
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:46,160
And I can take everything away from you.

128
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:05,320
I thought you'd stay
and look for your brother.

129
00:14:07,120 --> 00:14:09,200
Mom wants me to go home.

130
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:11,440
I'd actually like to stay longer.

131
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:13,840
I don't think that's a good idea.

132
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:16,600
You should go home and recover.

133
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:20,840
Ms. Alyssa.

134
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:23,480
Please go back to your room.

135
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:26,480
That way, I won't
have to worry about you too.

136
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:29,960
I'll let you know
as soon as there's any news.

137
00:14:36,400 --> 00:14:37,440
Come on, Korn.

138
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:13,920
Hello, Korn.

139
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:17,200
How are you feeling?

140
00:15:17,920 --> 00:15:20,120
The bullet just grazed my arm.

141
00:15:21,840 --> 00:15:23,120
I'm sorry

142
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:25,280
I couldn't save Wee.

143
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:31,680
Oh, dear.

144
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:34,560
It's okay, son.

145
00:15:37,120 --> 00:15:39,160
You did your best.

146
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:43,280
I just pray

147
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:46,280
that Wee will be safe.

148
00:15:48,400 --> 00:15:50,560
Wee is a good person.

149
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:54,840
I believe he'll be okay.

150
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:01,800
Yes.

151
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:07,920
Wee fell off the cliff…

152
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,040
because he was trying to save me.

153
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:21,360
If you hear anything about Wee,

154
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:24,600
call me right away, okay?

155
00:16:25,880 --> 00:16:26,880
I will, Mom.

156
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:32,960
Wee, my dear.

157
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:35,120
Please be okay.

158
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:37,600
You have to be safe, son.

159
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:17,839
MR. THAMRONG

160
00:17:24,079 --> 00:17:27,280
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Welcome to the callback service.</font></font></i>

161
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:37,160
Oh no.

162
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:44,480
Wee, please be okay.

163
00:17:52,800 --> 00:17:54,040
Don't die, Wee.

164
00:17:57,920 --> 00:17:59,360
Please don't die.

165
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:18,640
They've found a body.

166
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:49,680
Mr. Jak.

167
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:05,280
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Authorities have confirmed</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">that the deceased is Jak Kittikan,</font></font></i>

168
00:19:05,360 --> 00:19:08,720
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">owner of the famous Sun Secrets resort</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">on Tawan Island.</font></font></i>

169
00:19:17,120 --> 00:19:19,720
I never thought
he'd end up dying like this.

170
00:19:21,840 --> 00:19:23,200
I'm sorry for your loss.

171
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:27,960
He brought it on himself.

172
00:19:31,320 --> 00:19:32,360
Ms. Pat.

173
00:19:33,840 --> 00:19:35,240
Please arrange the funeral.

174
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:37,400
Of course.

175
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:42,440
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Meanwhile, Rawee Wittayadumrong,</font></font></i>

176
00:19:42,520 --> 00:19:45,840
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">who fell off the cliff, is still missing.</font></font></i>

177
00:19:45,920 --> 00:19:48,240
URGENT SEARCH FOR RAWEE WITTAYADUMRONG
AFTER FALL AT TAWAN ISLAND VIEWPOINT

178
00:20:02,280 --> 00:20:03,200
What are you doing here?

179
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,600
I came to congratulate you

180
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:16,600
on making it out alive.

181
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:20,000
Too bad

182
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:22,760
you weren't the one
who fell off that cliff.

183
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:26,240
I'd love to see Da lose someone
for a change.

184
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:29,160
That would be hilarious.

185
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:32,760
Hey, if you've got nothing nice to say,

186
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:33,760
just leave.

187
00:20:34,560 --> 00:20:35,520
Hold on.

188
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:37,840
What's the rush?

189
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:42,240
Still got those shares?

190
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:47,640
Hang on to them.

191
00:20:49,040 --> 00:20:51,160
I'll take you to trade them
for some bubble tea.

192
00:20:52,640 --> 00:20:53,720
You might get

193
00:20:54,840 --> 00:20:55,960
a couple of cups.

194
00:20:56,640 --> 00:20:57,880
I'll report you to the police.

195
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:03,920
Go ahead. Be my guest.

196
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:06,080
But before you do,

197
00:21:06,760 --> 00:21:08,280
ask your mother about something.

198
00:21:09,360 --> 00:21:11,920
I hear she recently met
with one of our competitors.

199
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:13,920
Hey.

200
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:17,280
What do you think would happen

201
00:21:18,440 --> 00:21:19,800
if the board found out?

202
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:23,000
I don't care.

203
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:24,840
Of course you don't.

204
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:28,000
She's not your real mother.

205
00:21:29,120 --> 00:21:30,240
That's why you don't care.

206
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:32,840
I get it.

207
00:21:34,320 --> 00:21:38,000
Looks like you'll soon be back
to scraping by with your real mother.

208
00:21:38,640 --> 00:21:41,680
What are you talking about? I'm a Tayawat!

209
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:44,680
Listen, kid.

210
00:21:46,080 --> 00:21:47,600
I've been lying my whole life.

211
00:21:48,440 --> 00:21:50,920
Nobody in the Tayawat family
is a better liar than me.

212
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:54,720
So don't try to bullshit me.

213
00:21:55,880 --> 00:21:58,160
I can tell you're not the real heir.

214
00:22:28,840 --> 00:22:30,040
You know,

215
00:22:30,920 --> 00:22:33,520
I really envy you and Korn.

216
00:22:34,840 --> 00:22:36,600
You have each other to lean on.

217
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:40,920
I feel like

218
00:22:41,640 --> 00:22:42,800
I'm all alone.

219
00:22:43,480 --> 00:22:45,600
Like I have to fight everything by myself.

220
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,200
Then just think of me

221
00:22:59,240 --> 00:23:01,120
as an older brother.

222
00:23:14,200 --> 00:23:17,640
Sometimes I wish I'd been born a man.

223
00:23:18,520 --> 00:23:19,920
Maybe I'd be stronger,

224
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:22,600
and Dad wouldn't have to worry so much.

225
00:23:36,400 --> 00:23:38,280
Do you have anything
you'd like to confess?

226
00:23:40,600 --> 00:23:41,600
I love you.

227
00:23:43,080 --> 00:23:44,040
What?

228
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:50,360
Is that what you wanted me to confess?

229
00:23:58,200 --> 00:23:59,640
You like me, don't you?

230
00:24:02,240 --> 00:24:04,080
You keep coming around
and using this as an excuse.

231
00:24:05,080 --> 00:24:06,800
You did all this because you like me,
didn't you?

232
00:24:10,440 --> 00:24:11,600
What if I said I do?

233
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:15,640
Then I'd tell you
I don't feel the same way.

234
00:24:21,240 --> 00:24:24,440
If that's all, I'll be going.

235
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:26,720
Okay, Wee.

236
00:24:27,320 --> 00:24:28,520
Don't call me that again.

237
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:32,520
You're the one who told me
to think of you as an older brother.

238
00:24:33,280 --> 00:24:35,800
-Call me what you did before.
-Okay, Wee.

239
00:24:56,680 --> 00:25:01,760
TAWAN ISLAND TEMPLE

240
00:25:09,120 --> 00:25:11,000
Hey, mister!

241
00:25:12,560 --> 00:25:13,520
Mister!

242
00:25:32,880 --> 00:25:34,560
Who saved me last night?

243
00:25:35,320 --> 00:25:37,200
Uncle Daeng. He's a local fisherman.

244
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:41,080
He regularly brings fish to the abbot.

245
00:25:42,840 --> 00:25:45,560
Did you try to kill yourself?

246
00:25:51,360 --> 00:25:52,240
No.

247
00:25:54,400 --> 00:25:55,920
I accidentally fell off a cliff.

248
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:57,400
You're lucky

249
00:25:57,480 --> 00:26:00,520
Uncle Daeng was out catching squid.

250
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:03,560
He saw you struggling and about to drown,

251
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:05,080
so he rescued you just in time.

252
00:26:05,680 --> 00:26:07,400
Where can I find Uncle Daeng?

253
00:26:08,640 --> 00:26:09,920
-Well…
-I want to thank him.

254
00:26:12,720 --> 00:26:16,480
Go to the pier and ask for Uncle Daeng.
Everyone knows him.

255
00:26:17,760 --> 00:26:19,200
Wait here.

256
00:26:19,280 --> 00:26:21,040
I'll get you something to eat.

257
00:26:31,640 --> 00:26:33,120
Thanks for calling to let me know.

258
00:26:33,200 --> 00:26:35,320
I'll take it from here. Okay.

259
00:26:37,520 --> 00:26:38,560
Ms. Alyssa.

260
00:26:39,160 --> 00:26:41,840
One of my men just called.
People at the market are saying

261
00:26:41,920 --> 00:26:43,680
someone was rescued
from drowning last night.

262
00:26:46,320 --> 00:26:47,320
Wee?

263
00:26:47,400 --> 00:26:49,640
It might be him, but we're not sure.

264
00:26:50,160 --> 00:26:51,200
Don't worry.

265
00:26:51,280 --> 00:26:53,680
I'll have my men here
help with the search too.

266
00:26:54,560 --> 00:26:55,600
Your men here?

267
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:00,880
They have a lot of connections
around here. They'll be a big help.

268
00:27:03,360 --> 00:27:06,440
There's a lot I don't know about you,
Uncle Thamrong.

269
00:27:08,680 --> 00:27:09,720
Yes.

270
00:27:49,800 --> 00:27:54,400
ENTER PASSCODE

271
00:27:58,920 --> 00:28:00,840
One, two, three.

272
00:28:02,720 --> 00:28:03,560
HAPPY BIRTHDAY, PHAKORN

273
00:28:50,880 --> 00:28:53,640
NADA TAYAWAT - TAWAN ISLAND TEMPLE

274
00:30:01,480 --> 00:30:04,200
-<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">When did you get back?</font></font></i>
-A little while ago.

275
00:30:04,280 --> 00:30:06,200
I came to see you as soon as I was done.

276
00:30:06,280 --> 00:30:09,160
You can't tell anyone
we're secretly meeting.

277
00:30:10,560 --> 00:30:12,600
We look more alike
as we get older, don't we?

278
00:30:13,680 --> 00:30:14,520
Yes.

279
00:30:15,640 --> 00:30:19,080
Why don't we get a few matching outfits?

280
00:30:19,680 --> 00:30:21,760
We never had matching clothes
when we were little.

281
00:30:23,560 --> 00:30:24,480
Okay.

282
00:30:26,200 --> 00:30:29,720
You've come back just in time.
I'm getting married.

283
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:34,120
-Married?
-Yes.

284
00:30:35,720 --> 00:30:38,480
I just want to get out of that house.

285
00:30:41,880 --> 00:30:43,000
Why?

286
00:30:43,880 --> 00:30:46,640
Are you really that unhappy living there?

287
00:30:47,520 --> 00:30:49,640
I can't even be myself.

288
00:30:51,320 --> 00:30:52,640
I don't even get to choose

289
00:30:53,680 --> 00:30:55,360
who I love.

290
00:30:55,960 --> 00:30:58,080
But you said you're getting married.

291
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:00,760
Father agreed to let me marry him.

292
00:31:01,640 --> 00:31:03,640
But he won't let us register our marriage.

293
00:31:03,720 --> 00:31:05,360
And we have to move away.

294
00:31:06,160 --> 00:31:08,560
It's like he's disowned me.

295
00:31:09,240 --> 00:31:11,000
Why doesn't he like your boyfriend?

296
00:31:12,080 --> 00:31:13,160
Because he's poor.

297
00:31:15,600 --> 00:31:17,920
And all the relatives
have turned against me too.

298
00:31:19,280 --> 00:31:20,800
Everyone hates me.

299
00:31:21,840 --> 00:31:25,240
So you'd rather struggle
with the man you love?

300
00:31:27,560 --> 00:31:28,480
Yes.

301
00:31:37,720 --> 00:31:39,080
Mr. Rawich is waiting for me.

302
00:31:46,080 --> 00:31:47,000
Don't tell him about me.

303
00:31:47,880 --> 00:31:50,800
I won't. I should get going.

304
00:31:52,200 --> 00:31:55,120
I've had such a wonderful time today.

305
00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:57,000
So have I.

306
00:31:58,200 --> 00:31:59,400
See you again.

307
00:32:04,880 --> 00:32:05,920
Mr. Rawich.

308
00:32:07,320 --> 00:32:08,560
Have you been waiting long?

309
00:32:08,640 --> 00:32:10,920
Not at all. Let me help you carry that.

310
00:32:44,680 --> 00:32:45,920
Conference Room Two.

311
00:32:46,720 --> 00:32:47,760
I'll be right there.

312
00:32:57,000 --> 00:32:58,320
Who are you really?

313
00:32:58,400 --> 00:33:00,320
What's got you so curious all of a sudden?

314
00:33:02,080 --> 00:33:06,080
What are you planning to do with Tayawat?
Why did you meet with our competitor?

315
00:33:07,680 --> 00:33:09,800
Why don't you worry
about saving your own skin first?

316
00:33:09,880 --> 00:33:11,480
Stop sticking your nose into my business.

317
00:33:12,040 --> 00:33:15,240
What I do with Tayawat
is none of your concern.

318
00:33:16,160 --> 00:33:18,680
But what you do affects me.

319
00:33:19,520 --> 00:33:20,560
Of course it does.

320
00:33:21,240 --> 00:33:24,320
You're pretending to be my son, after all.

321
00:33:26,560 --> 00:33:29,320
Look, I don't want to get
into any more trouble.

322
00:33:31,080 --> 00:33:32,720
It can't get any worse.

323
00:33:33,320 --> 00:33:35,720
You're already in as deep as you can get.

324
00:33:45,840 --> 00:33:47,040
You and Uncle Thamrong

325
00:33:47,880 --> 00:33:50,000
are working together
on something, aren't you?

326
00:33:53,560 --> 00:33:55,760
Then what Wee saw must be true.

327
00:33:57,120 --> 00:33:58,840
He saw the two of you

328
00:33:59,680 --> 00:34:00,720
embracing.

329
00:34:04,120 --> 00:34:05,600
You've gotten what you wanted.

330
00:34:06,280 --> 00:34:09,280
So you'd better keep your mouth shut.
Don't go looking for trouble.

331
00:34:11,520 --> 00:34:12,880
I haven't gotten

332
00:34:14,360 --> 00:34:15,560
everything I want yet.

333
00:34:18,159 --> 00:34:19,800
Don't get too greedy, Phakorn.

334
00:34:20,520 --> 00:34:22,320
Even with Rawee gone,

335
00:34:22,400 --> 00:34:25,320
there are still ways to prove

336
00:34:25,400 --> 00:34:27,400
you're not a real Tayawat.

337
00:34:27,480 --> 00:34:30,600
I've already gotten rid
of the real Tayawat heirs.

338
00:34:31,199 --> 00:34:34,040
Getting rid of you would be even easier.

339
00:34:35,920 --> 00:34:37,199
Stop threatening me.

340
00:34:37,280 --> 00:34:40,600
I've come too far
to be scared of something like this.

341
00:34:42,239 --> 00:34:43,080
Get out.

342
00:34:44,960 --> 00:34:46,120
Get out!

343
00:34:53,480 --> 00:34:54,880
Taddao!

344
00:34:54,960 --> 00:34:56,080
Yes, ma'am?

345
00:34:58,160 --> 00:34:59,120
Go find out

346
00:35:00,480 --> 00:35:03,200
how Phakorn learned about SL Company.

347
00:35:03,280 --> 00:35:04,480
Yes, ma'am.

348
00:35:43,240 --> 00:35:45,440
MS. ALYSSA

349
00:36:12,280 --> 00:36:13,120
What is it?

350
00:36:14,200 --> 00:36:17,520
I knew it. I knew you'd have Wee's phone.

351
00:36:19,840 --> 00:36:21,280
I never thought

352
00:36:22,080 --> 00:36:23,880
you'd choose to call Wee

353
00:36:24,720 --> 00:36:26,200
instead of me.

354
00:36:27,840 --> 00:36:29,960
I don't think
we have anything left to talk about.

355
00:36:32,040 --> 00:36:32,920
Why?

356
00:36:33,600 --> 00:36:35,240
Are you breaking up with me?

357
00:36:37,760 --> 00:36:39,240
You know why.

358
00:36:40,600 --> 00:36:42,680
So now that I'm not a Tayawat,

359
00:36:43,360 --> 00:36:45,080
you're just going to toss me aside?

360
00:36:48,080 --> 00:36:49,760
I don't care

361
00:36:49,840 --> 00:36:52,000
whether you or Wee is the real heir.

362
00:36:52,680 --> 00:36:55,720
Stop picking a fight.
Why do you have Wee's phone?

363
00:36:56,520 --> 00:36:58,320
Are you trying to destroy evidence?

364
00:36:58,920 --> 00:37:02,400
Hey, can't we just talk
without arguing, Alyssa?

365
00:37:03,520 --> 00:37:04,520
Fine.

366
00:37:06,160 --> 00:37:07,840
I just called to tell you

367
00:37:08,560 --> 00:37:10,920
that a fisherman rescued
someone from the water last night.

368
00:37:13,920 --> 00:37:15,080
You mean Wee?

369
00:37:17,960 --> 00:37:19,440
I hope so.

370
00:37:20,800 --> 00:37:22,400
Then we'll finally know the truth

371
00:37:23,800 --> 00:37:25,240
about what happened on that cliff.

372
00:37:34,200 --> 00:37:35,520
Instead of being suspicious of me,

373
00:37:36,400 --> 00:37:39,200
you should be wary
of Uncle Thamrong and your Aunt Da.

374
00:37:40,160 --> 00:37:42,120
Those two are closer than you realize.

375
00:37:44,800 --> 00:37:45,920
That's ridiculous.

376
00:37:47,080 --> 00:37:49,080
Wee saw them embracing

377
00:37:49,160 --> 00:37:51,280
at Ms. Nada's house.

378
00:37:53,240 --> 00:37:56,000
Those two aren't as trustworthy
as you think.

379
00:40:06,920 --> 00:40:10,040
One of our staff members really did see
Thong take Mr. Jak away.

380
00:40:11,160 --> 00:40:14,400
Thong? The worker at Ms. Nada's house?

381
00:40:15,080 --> 00:40:19,400
Yes. Thong's a freak.
We're all scared of him.

382
00:40:22,400 --> 00:40:24,200
Does he have any relatives?

383
00:40:25,680 --> 00:40:27,720
There's only Ms. Nada.

384
00:40:27,800 --> 00:40:31,480
I don't know where he could be hiding.
Everyone on the island knows him.

385
00:43:52,480 --> 00:43:53,720
Ms. Nada has already left.

386
00:43:56,000 --> 00:43:57,440
What brings you here, Ms. Alyssa?

387
00:44:02,120 --> 00:44:04,000
I'm glad you're here, Uncle.

388
00:44:04,080 --> 00:44:05,720
You have a key to the house, don't you?

389
00:44:06,360 --> 00:44:09,080
I want to look for evidence
related to Thong.

390
00:44:11,360 --> 00:44:13,320
He has no relatives,

391
00:44:13,400 --> 00:44:14,880
and everyone here knows him.

392
00:44:14,960 --> 00:44:17,680
He might be hiding in this house.

393
00:44:20,760 --> 00:44:22,680
I think you should go back to the resort.

394
00:44:23,360 --> 00:44:25,760
It's best to leave the search for Thong
to the police.

395
00:44:28,680 --> 00:44:30,560
Are you protecting your man?

396
00:44:36,160 --> 00:44:38,080
Or is there someone else
you're protecting?

397
00:44:42,040 --> 00:44:43,440
What are you talking about?

398
00:44:51,160 --> 00:44:52,960
Nothing stays secret forever.

399
00:44:55,200 --> 00:44:57,640
Are you and Aunt Da

400
00:44:59,360 --> 00:45:00,400
seeing each other?

401
00:45:34,520 --> 00:45:35,400
Get out.

402
00:45:37,280 --> 00:45:38,320
I said, get out!

403
00:46:06,440 --> 00:46:09,760
Wee saw you and Aunt Da embracing here.

404
00:46:11,560 --> 00:46:12,600
Is that true?

405
00:46:19,800 --> 00:46:21,800
And there's the matter of Ms. Pimpa.

406
00:46:24,520 --> 00:46:26,960
What does Ms. Pimpa have to do with this?

407
00:46:27,760 --> 00:46:30,480
You know exactly
what she has to do with it.

408
00:46:34,640 --> 00:46:36,680
Ms. Alyssa, I'm completely confused.

409
00:46:39,800 --> 00:46:40,840
Look at this.

410
00:47:43,040 --> 00:47:44,080
Oh no.

411
00:47:45,960 --> 00:47:47,720
What happened here?

412
00:48:34,640 --> 00:48:35,840
I think

413
00:48:37,080 --> 00:48:39,520
it's time you told me the truth, Uncle.

414
00:49:24,840 --> 00:49:25,840
Let me go already.

415
00:49:26,960 --> 00:49:28,320
I don't want to hurt you.

416
00:49:29,440 --> 00:49:30,800
I'm not going anywhere

417
00:49:31,680 --> 00:49:33,560
until you tell me the whole truth.

418
00:49:35,120 --> 00:49:38,520
Want to know what terrible things
your grandfather did?

419
00:49:39,320 --> 00:49:40,520
Who are you talking about?

420
00:49:41,640 --> 00:49:43,240
That bastard Prajak!

421
00:49:43,320 --> 00:49:45,440
And I know who your parents are.

422
00:49:49,200 --> 00:49:51,120
Help! Fire!

423
00:49:51,200 --> 00:49:53,520
Fire! Help! Somebody help!

424
00:49:55,240 --> 00:49:56,920
Thong, get Nada out now!

425
00:49:57,000 --> 00:49:58,080
Wait here, Aunt Nuan!

426
00:49:58,160 --> 00:49:59,880
-Come on!
-Take care of her!

427
00:50:02,640 --> 00:50:05,320
Thong! Get Nada out now!

428
00:50:08,200 --> 00:50:10,120
Nada, run!

429
00:50:12,080 --> 00:50:13,520
Aah!

430
00:50:14,120 --> 00:50:15,400
My face is like this

431
00:50:15,920 --> 00:50:18,160
because that bastard Prajak
burned down our village.

432
00:50:18,240 --> 00:50:21,720
Someone I loved died in the fire.
I couldn't save her in time.

433
00:50:21,800 --> 00:50:25,680
But karma is real.
His wife died in a fire too.

434
00:50:31,840 --> 00:50:33,800
You saved my mother, Thong?

435
00:50:35,080 --> 00:50:36,240
I didn't save her.

436
00:50:37,200 --> 00:50:38,760
And she wasn't your mother either.

437
00:50:39,600 --> 00:50:42,480
Prajak took your mother away
long before that.

438
00:50:43,120 --> 00:50:45,160
And he didn't even know
he had two daughters.

439
00:50:58,720 --> 00:50:59,680
My mother had a twin?

440
00:51:02,400 --> 00:51:03,280
Yes.

441
00:51:08,240 --> 00:51:09,480
Then which one is my mother?

442
00:51:17,080 --> 00:51:18,880
Aunt Da has a twin?

443
00:51:19,960 --> 00:51:21,240
Yes.

444
00:51:22,120 --> 00:51:23,600
You can't tell them apart.

445
00:51:25,960 --> 00:51:28,720
Ms. Lada switched places
to fool Mr. Rawich.

446
00:51:29,320 --> 00:51:30,400
So the Aunt Da

447
00:51:31,120 --> 00:51:32,520
I've known all this time

448
00:51:33,680 --> 00:51:35,280
is actually Ms. Lada?

449
00:51:42,160 --> 00:51:43,520
Where is Ms. Nada now?

450
00:51:49,680 --> 00:51:51,640
MS. NADA

451
00:52:00,360 --> 00:52:03,200
I'm sorry to bother you.

452
00:52:03,920 --> 00:52:06,240
But I'm really worried.

453
00:52:07,920 --> 00:52:11,200
Mr. Thamrong has people looking for him.

454
00:52:11,280 --> 00:52:13,880
But they haven't found him yet.

455
00:52:16,240 --> 00:52:18,480
-I see.
-Well…

456
00:52:20,320 --> 00:52:23,240
Have you spoken to Korn?

457
00:52:24,400 --> 00:52:26,160
He hasn't answered any of my calls.

458
00:52:29,560 --> 00:52:31,960
If I see Phakorn, I'll let him know.

459
00:52:33,320 --> 00:52:36,800
And if there's any news,

460
00:52:36,880 --> 00:52:38,360
I'll tell you right away.

461
00:52:39,600 --> 00:52:40,720
Please don't worry.

462
00:52:42,360 --> 00:52:43,520
Thank you.

463
00:52:58,760 --> 00:53:00,680
PHAKORN

464
00:53:46,760 --> 00:53:51,000
Korn, hurry and pull me up!
I can't hold on much longer.

465
00:54:35,040 --> 00:54:36,960
PHAKORN

466
00:54:39,200 --> 00:54:41,800
Korn! I've called you so many times.
Why didn't you answer?

467
00:54:42,400 --> 00:54:43,520
I didn't want to.

468
00:54:44,880 --> 00:54:46,760
Everyone keeps asking about Wee.

469
00:54:47,680 --> 00:54:48,960
I have no answers.

470
00:54:50,240 --> 00:54:54,160
Didn't you think about how worried I'd be?

471
00:54:54,840 --> 00:54:55,920
Worried about who?

472
00:54:58,320 --> 00:54:59,480
Me?

473
00:55:02,040 --> 00:55:03,200
Or Wee?

474
00:55:03,880 --> 00:55:05,600
Hey, Korn!

475
00:55:06,240 --> 00:55:07,880
Why would you say that?

476
00:55:08,680 --> 00:55:11,680
We don't even know if Wee's alive or dead.

477
00:55:13,880 --> 00:55:15,960
Everyone's so worried about Wee.

478
00:55:17,680 --> 00:55:21,640
Has anyone even asked how I'm doing?

479
00:55:23,720 --> 00:55:25,880
I got shot too, Mom.

480
00:55:28,480 --> 00:55:30,000
If I'd died

481
00:55:31,320 --> 00:55:33,880
instead of Wee,

482
00:55:35,280 --> 00:55:37,400
everyone would be happier, wouldn't they?

483
00:56:48,240 --> 00:56:51,960
I don't know.
I get their names mixed up too.

484
00:56:54,400 --> 00:56:55,840
And the woman who was just here?

485
00:56:56,600 --> 00:56:57,440
Who was she?

486
00:56:59,240 --> 00:57:01,640
Lada, your aunt.

487
00:57:04,520 --> 00:57:05,920
Nada, your mother,

488
00:57:06,560 --> 00:57:07,600
died a long time ago.

489
00:57:15,040 --> 00:57:16,600
How did my mother die?

490
00:57:23,000 --> 00:57:24,320
How did my mother die?

491
00:57:40,040 --> 00:57:41,960
Did you kill my mother, Thong?

492
00:57:42,560 --> 00:57:46,440
Rawee isn't your son either.
Who are those two, really?

493
00:57:46,520 --> 00:57:48,440
Why did you bring them into my family?

494
00:57:48,520 --> 00:57:51,080
No wonder you've been asleep for so long.

495
00:57:52,560 --> 00:57:56,120
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">How long have you known</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">about Ms. Nada, Uncle?</font></font></i>

496
00:57:56,200 --> 00:57:57,840
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">We've been together all this time.</font></font></i>

497
00:57:58,600 --> 00:58:00,440
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Even if she used me, I'd accept it.</font></font></i>

498
00:58:01,520 --> 00:58:04,000
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Because I've already fallen in love</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">with her.</font></font></i>

499
00:58:07,720 --> 00:58:11,440
-My place is a bit cramped.
-I just need a roof over my head.

500
00:58:11,520 --> 00:58:14,560
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">If you want me to help you,</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">tell me what's going on.</font></font></i>

501
00:58:17,720 --> 00:58:18,880
Who is that?

502
00:58:18,960 --> 00:58:20,080
Wee?

503
00:59:07,120 --> 00:59:09,960
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
